How to Become a Verified Technician on Mekh: Complete Guide
Introduction
Mekh is Kenya's leading automotive services marketplace that connects car owners with verified professional technicians across Nairobi and beyond. If you have expertise in automotive services like window tinting, car wrapping, ceramic coating, or mechanical repairs, becoming a verified technician on Mekh opens up new business opportunities and helps you reach more customers.

This comprehensive guide walks you through the entire process of signing up, building your profile, and getting verified on the Mekh platform. From initial registration to going live, we'll cover every step with detailed instructions and tips for success.

Step 1: Access the Technician Registration Page
Getting Started
Visit Mekh: Go to mekh.app in your web browser
Navigate to Registration: Click on "Join as Technician" or visit /join directly
Authentication Required: You'll be redirected to sign in with your Google account or create a new account
User Account Creation: If you don't have an account, create one with your email and password
Account Requirements
Valid Email: Required for account verification and notifications
Google OAuth: Recommended for easier login and account security
Phone Number: Will be collected during profile setup for client communications
Step 2: Complete the Profile Setup 
Mekh uses a 7-step to guide you through profile creation. Each step saves automatically, so you can return later if needed. Let's go through each step:

Step 1: Personal & Business Information
Required Fields:

First Name & Last Name: Your legal names
Business Name: Your company or trading name (e.g., "John's Auto Detailing")
Phone Number: Active Kenyan number for client communications (e.g., 0712345678)
Experience Level: Select from options like "1-2 years", "3-5 years", "6-10 years", "10+ years"
Area/Location: Your primary service area (e.g., "Westlands, Nairobi")
Optional but Recommended:

Bio/Description: Write a compelling description of your services and expertise. Be specific about what you do, how long you've been doing it, and why clients should choose you.
Pro Tip: Write your bio conversationally, like you're talking to a potential client. Include specific details about your experience and what makes you stand out.

Step 2: Location & Service Mobility
Location Details:

Area Confirmation: Re-confirm your service area
Google Maps Link: Optional - paste a Google Maps link to your business location
Automatic Geocoding: The system can extract coordinates from your Maps link
Mobile Service: Choose whether you provide mobile services:
No: You work at a fixed location only
Yes: You travel to clients
Both: You offer both mobile and studio services
Location Benefits: Including precise location helps clients find nearby technicians and improves your visibility in location-based searches.

Step 3: Business Hours
Operating Schedule:

Set your availability for each day of the week
Mark days as "Open" or "Closed"
Set specific opening and closing times
Enable "Available on Request" for flexible scheduling (recommended for most technicians)
Default Setup: The system starts with all days closed - you'll need to configure your actual hours.

Tip: Be realistic about your availability. Clients appreciate accurate scheduling information.

Step 4: Services Offered
Service Selection (1-4 Services Maximum): Choose from Mekh's comprehensive service list:

Body & Exterior: Window Tinting, Car Wrapping, PPF Installation, Ceramic Coating, Car Buffing, Chrome Deleting, Rim Customization
Electricals & Security: Car Audio Systems, Security Systems, Key Programming, ECU Tuning, Lighting Upgrades
Mechanical & Repair: Engine Diagnostics, Brake Services, Suspension Work, Tire Services, Oil Changes
Interior & Detailing: Car Detailing, Upholstery Work, Carpet Cleaning, Interior Trim
Pricing Setup:

Window Tinting: Special pricing for different tint types (Chameleon, Ceramic, 3M, Llumar, Local)
Other Services: Set base prices and mark as "Negotiable" if flexible
Service Variants: These are services that appear under one major service which is very bold, for example : car audio installation is a very large service and not all clients would the full service but some would like something like equalizer installation or android screen installation, so that where the service variants come under.
Whenever you click the add service variant button there will be no an overall price for the particular service but you will be entering the price of each service variant.
Service Notes: Add details about pricing variables (e.g., "Price varies by vehicle size" or the factors featuring the service variant/ service)
Service Category Assignment: Each service must be assigned to one of four categories for proper search filtering.
Also after selecting/adding the services you offer select a primary from the listed ones, the primary service should a service that you are very well skilled in and also you have alot of experience offering that service.
Only one service should qualify for the primary service.
Strategic Advice:

Select 2-3 services to start - this attracts more bookings than specializing in just one
Price competitively but realistically
Mark services as negotiable if you have flexibility
Step 5: Portfolio Photos (Minimum 2 Required)
Photo Requirements:

Upload at least 2 high-quality photos of your work
Maximum 6 photos allowed
Supported formats: JPEG, PNG, WebP
Images are automatically optimized and stored in the database.
Photo Suggestions:

Before/after shots showing your work quality
Close-ups of detailing work
Full vehicle transformations
Professional equipment and workspace
Team photos or business branding
Technical Notes:

Images are compressed and optimized automatically
File size limits apply - keep images under 5MB each
Step 6: TikTok Videos (Optional)
Video Integration:

Add up to 3 TikTok video links
Videos showcase your work process and quality
Supported: TikTok URLs only (YouTube/Instagram coming soon)
URL Formats Supported:

https://tiktok.com/@username/video/1234567890
https://tiktok.com/v/1234567890
https://vm.tiktok.com/ABC123

Video Benefits:
Builds trust through visual proof of work
Appears on your profile for client viewing
Can improve conversion rates
Step 7: Pricing Notes (Optional)
Additional Information:

Add any extra pricing details, special offers, or terms
Mention bulk discounts, package deals, or seasonal promotions

Step 3: Profile Submission and Verification
Auto-Approval Process
Immediate Status: Unlike many platforms, Mekh auto-approves technician profiles for immediate visibility. Your profile goes live immediately after completion.

What Happens Next:

Profile Creation: Your information is saved to the database
Status Set to "Live": You can start receiving inquiries right away
Dashboard Access: You get access to your technician dashboard
Client Visibility: Your profile appears in search results
Verification Features
Trust Indicators:

Profile Verification Badge: Shows you're a registered technician
Service Categories: Properly categorized for accurate search results
Rating System: Client reviews build your reputation over time
Booking Tracking: All inquiries are logged and tracked
Step 4: Managing Your Technician Dashboard
Dashboard Features
Available After Registration:

Profile Management: Edit your information and services
Lead Management: View and respond to client inquiries
Booking Tracking: Monitor service requests and status updates
Review Monitoring: See client feedback and ratings
Analytics: Track your performance metrics
Lead Response Process
When Clients Book:

WhatsApp Integration: Clients are directed to WhatsApp for communication
Lead Notifications: You receive email notifications of new inquiries
Client Information: Access client details, service requests, and vehicle information
Status Updates: Mark leads as "Pending", "Job Done", or "Not Converted".
When the status on the lead appears as 'pending' this means that you have received  a new client and you haven't communicated with them for their inquires.
'Job done'- indicates that you communicated with the technician and solved / implemented the services they wanted. Whenever you select and indiicae the status of the lead as Job Done it prompts the client who had booked you to leave a review/rating that will help you get more clients. Also when you select the lead staus as 'job done' you can't undo that selection.
'Not Converted'- you select this status in the leads if the client was not that interested to that service but they just inquiring. You can also be able to change this status if the same client reaches out for that service and they want it done.

Communication Guidelines
Best Practices:

